ratorname{ln}⁡(e)+2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}(1)+1,\\frac{1}{3}(1)+2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{7}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349071 13194139535436 true] [17592186349070 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535436 true] [17592186349070 1041 "field-1" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349070 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349071 13194139535436 true] [17592186349070 1110 #uuid "507e8bbe-d8e6-535e-a453-e72c66d52a71" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349071 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349071 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349071 1111 #uuid "1134dff4-d10e-507a-877e-b2caecff1441" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349072 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349073 13194139535436 true] [17592186349072 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535436 true] [17592186349072 1041 "field-2" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349072 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349073 13194139535436 true] [17592186349072 1110 #uuid "f2b24eeb-d81f-5857-b049-841eb6fdcd06" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349073 1034 "\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349073 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349073 1111 #uuid "86dd3865-1575-5660-bdd6-f39f8915596b" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349074 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349075 13194139535436 true] [17592186349074 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349078 13194139535436 true] [17592186349074 1089 "q-351156" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349074 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535436 true] [17592186349074 1100 "The velocity $v$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nv(t)=⟨6{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}⟩,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $r=⟨-1,\\,2⟩$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position of $P$ at time $t=1.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$r(1)=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349074 1113 #uuid "16b5c9a0-af08-5610-93fc-777e421047d8" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349074 1145 "To compute the position vector, we need to integrate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨6{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{t}^{3}+{C}_{1},\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $r(0)=⟨-1,2⟩.$ Substituting $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨2(0)^{3}+{C}_{1},\\,\\sqrt{(0)^{3}}+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨-1,2⟩ & =⟨{C}_{1},\\,{C}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have ${C}_{1}=-1$ and ${C}_{2}=2.$ Therefore, the position vector at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2{t}^{3}-1,\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}+2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the position vector at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨2(1)^{3}-1,\\,\\sqrt{(1)^{3}}+2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-1,\\,1+2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349075 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349076 13194139535436 true] [17592186349075 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349077 13194139535436 true] [17592186349075 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535436 true] [17592186349075 1041 "field-1" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349075 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349077 13194139535436 true] [17592186349075 1110 #uuid "da301ea8-60db-506d-b761-d4949bbcb7e4" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349076 1034 "2" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349076 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349076 1111 #uuid "70bb012f-e31e-5015-9036-ff294521e2cb" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349077 1034 "1" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349077 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349077 1111 #uuid "70da22fc-edeb-5404-907d-601a23b1f379" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349078 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349079 13194139535436 true] [17592186349078 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535436 true] [17592186349078 1041 "field-2" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349078 1