ned}\n$$\n\nTo find the times at which the particle is at the origin, we solve the equation $r(t)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{t}^{2}-3t+2,\\,{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-3t+2 & =(t-1)(t-2)=0\\,⇒\\,t=1,2, \\\\ {t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+2t & =t(t-1)(t-2)=0\\,⇒\\,t=0,1,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values of $t$ that satisfy both equations are $t=1$ and $t=2.$ \n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the particle is at the origin when\n$t=1$ and $t=2.$" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349090 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349091 13194139535436 true] [17592186349090 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535436 true] [17592186349090 1041 "field-1" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349090 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349091 13194139535436 true] [17592186349090 1110 #uuid "1135dfc6-61f9-5317-bd23-2b1fac3e1364" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349091 1034 "1" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349091 1111 #uuid "6daa03a0-6e36-5190-b931-63a181dd9164" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349093 13194139535436 true] [17592186349092 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535436 true] [17592186349092 1041 "field-2" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349092 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349093 13194139535436 true] [17592186349092 1110 #uuid "7f162848-7673-5f82-8700-a5a6f6e7baa8" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349093 1034 "2" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349093 1111 #uuid "23601914-deb3-5fd3-bd8a-7d78dc847324" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349094 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349095 13194139535436 true] [17592186349094 1089 "q-351517" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349094 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535436 true] [17592186349094 1100 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na(t)=⟨48(2t+1)^{2},\\,-6⟩.\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle is at the position $(2,-1)$ and has velocit