t satisfy both equations are $t=\\pm 1.$ Therefore, we conclude that the particle is at the origin  when $t=\\pm 1.$" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349137 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349138 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349139 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349140 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349141 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1041 "selection" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349141 13194139535436 true] [17592186349136 1110 #uuid "cd9bae5e-c1f7-5f0e-bbc6-93b1a892de41" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349137 1034 "t=-1,0" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349137 1111 #uuid "d71a824c-ac8d-53c3-b0c4-a3739a9d260a" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349138 1034 "The particle is never at the origin" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535436 true] [17592186349138 1111 #uuid "32f39688-e268-5291-9614-70f19cc40505" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349139 1034 "t=\\pm 1,0" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349139 1111 #uuid "4501016f-905c-512b-9459-840c2c83b03a" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349140 1034 "t=0,1" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349140 1111 #uuid "3bdc7dce-3956-5f91-822d-4d739f9ad379" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349141 1034 "t=\\pm 1" 13194139535436 true] [17592186349141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535436 true] [17592186349141 1111 #uuid "e5fd1c43-1d86-5cb4-b74d-bf8ddf640bb8" 13194139535436 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-122422" 17592186349035 "q-122422/selection" 17592186349036 "q-122422/selection/0fdcb6c0298ea155769523771cf53ad06bde8d047c9429e2c3a1ea0bc5e184e7" 17592186349037 "q-122422/selection/12a192